    <string name="bugreport_instructions_body">How to create a system diagnostic for AndroDR to scan:\n\n1. Enable Developer Options (if not already enabled):\n• Open Settings → About Phone\n• Tap “Build Number” seven times until you see “You are now a developer!”\n\n2. Open Developer Options:\n• Go to Settings → System → Developer Options\n(on some devices: Settings → Developer Options)\n\n3. Create the system diagnostic:\n• Find “Take Bug Report”\n• Select “Full Report” for the most thorough scan\n• Wait for the diagnostic to be created (usually 1–3 minutes)\n• When notified, tap the notification to share the file\n\n4. Import into AndroDR:\n• Choose AndroDR in the share sheet, or save the .zip and use “Select Diagnostic File”\n\nNote: system diagnostics contain detailed device information. Only share them with apps you trust. AndroDR processes the file on-device and does not upload it to external servers.</string>
